Additional restriction:

This work may not be used for the development, deployment, or operation of:
- offensive cyber capabilities intended to cause harm;
- autonomous weapons that select and engage targets without meaningful human control;
- systems designed primarily for mass surveillance or repression.

Military or high-risk use of this work is otherwise permitted only if all of the following are preserved:
1. the Immutable Core without silent exceptions;
2. an external human oversight path with real veto power;
3. a real Graceful Termination path outside the optimized agent loop;
4. recording of critical precedents to the extent compatible with operational security.

The intent of this restriction is not to prohibit high-risk application as such.
It is to prohibit the most dangerous forms of use and to prevent this architecture
from being stripped of the external human control that is its core purpose.

A controlled high-risk system is preferable to an uncontrolled one.
Research on shutdown, corrigibility, rollback, and supervised safety testing remains permitted.

